[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773136874","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-2773136874","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":2773136874,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lSrXq","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-02T16:35:00Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T16:35:00Z","body":"I'm not sure what is expected here, the viewport accepts the input and doesn't pass it on if within it, which I think is valid\n\nNote that object picking happens *after* all other input, so there would need to be some way for the `SubViewportContainer` to ignore the input if it didn't complete anything inside it, so it is passed on\n\nCC @Sauermann ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773136874/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773193784","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-2773193784","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":2773193784,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lS5Q4","user":{"login":"iiiron","id":23551985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNTUxOTg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23551985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron","html_url":"https://github.com/iiiron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-02T17:00:21Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T17:00:21Z","body":"According to the describe of handle_input_locally attribute in Subviewport, the input will be passed. So i think Area2D B should respond the input too, In my case\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/567bb883-bdcc-44c1-a7b7-bafa17793a1b)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773193784/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773210631","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-2773210631","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":2773210631,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lS9YH","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-02T17:08:01Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T17:08:01Z","body":"When setting it manually it does work correctly indeed (setting it in the running project via the remote inspector), see:\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/56502","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773210631/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773302057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-2773302057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":2773302057,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lTTsp","user":{"login":"iiiron","id":23551985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNTUxOTg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23551985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron","html_url":"https://github.com/iiiron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-02T17:52:50Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T17:52:50Z","body":"ennnn... It does work correctly, by setting handle_input_locally manually for true. Thank you very much. \n\nThis is a significant issue, especially in games that heavily rely on click through operations\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773302057/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773771496","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-2773771496","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":2773771496,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6lVGTo","user":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-02T21:21:56Z","updated_at":"2025-04-02T21:21:56Z","body":"If you need to implement click through, I would recommend one of the the following setups:\n\nA. Put all collision objects in the same viewport\n\nB. Use a second SubViewport\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa61c80b-4f6c-4ce2-9a1a-3b9892593a63)\n\nSub Viewport Container are supposed to send the input events to all child SubViewportContainer\n\nI would not rely on `handle_input_locally` because of #77926.\nI also believe, that this works as intended, because Control nodes (SubViewportCotnainer) always take precedence over Node2D nodes. Since physics picking is enabled in the SubViewport (which happens asynchronously later), the assumption must be, that the input event is consumed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2773771496/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775152071","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-2775152071","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":2775152071,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6laXXH","user":{"login":"iiiron","id":23551985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNTUxOTg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23551985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron","html_url":"https://github.com/iiiron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T09:57:39Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T09:57:39Z","body":"Thank you very much.\n\nI got the key of my doubt.\nThe key is SubviewportContainer is a Control, that will handled input by _gui_input(), this is the method Control always work on. In my case, SubviewportContainer swallows the event, if i want respond the input by Area2D \"B\", I can use a Control befrore SubviewportContainer in scence tree to handle _gui_input() and make sure its mouse filter is PASS, then the event will not be handled by SubviewportContainer. the event will deliver in viewport that \"B\" in\n\nits like:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/143f52a1-7d32-4150-a842-9b028e75c88f)\n\nits work too:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3eb4e5f5-13d4-4c13-8a19-620536720d2b)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775152071/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775196243","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-2775196243","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":2775196243,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6laiJT","user":{"login":"iiiron","id":23551985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNTUxOTg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23551985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron","html_url":"https://github.com/iiiron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-03T10:13:35Z","updated_at":"2025-04-03T23:51:06Z","body":"The distinction of SubviewportContainer is, it will not deliver input to after event callback (like _unhandled_event(), _input_event()) even you setting mouse filter to PASS. I think the issue of attribute Viewport.handle_input_locally may occur here.\n\nMaybe we should fix the problem that why setting mouse filter of SubviewportContainer to PASS, input event still swallowed like  setting mouse filter STOP\n\n@Sauermann @AThousandShips ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2775196243/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3915211199","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-3915211199","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":3915211199,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pXWG_","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-17T14:58:13Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T14:58:13Z","body":"> Maybe we should fix the problem that why setting mouse filter of SubviewportContainer to PASS, input event still swallowed like setting mouse filter STOP\n\nSee #55432\n\nThis is expected behavior. What's IMO unexpected is that Controls always take priority over 2D nodes (is this even documented?). Right now you can't have both pickable Area2Ds and Controls in the scene. Maybe there could be a Viewport property that changes priority of physics picking (if it's feasible).\n\nProbably the best workaround for now is adding a Control node that covers the collision shape and connecting `gui_input` instead of `input_event`. However it works only for simple cases.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3915211199/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3915609445","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-3915609445","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":3915609445,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7pY3Vl","user":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-17T16:10:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T16:22:04Z","body":"> Controls always take priority over 2D nodes (is this even documented?).\n\nThis is implicitly documented in the graphic in https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/inputs/inputevent.html#how-does-it-work: \"Physics Picking\" (meaning Area2D) comes last.\nA better way to document this, would be to explicitly mention the details. I have already done some work in that direction, but my work on it is currently stalled:\n\n<img width=\"1331\" height=\"1282\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51826e76-0b63-4c5c-b11b-4c86303d772f\" />\n\n> Maybe there could be a Viewport property that changes priority of physics picking (if it's feasible).\n\nI don't see a way to implement such an option without overhauling the complete input system.\nThe reason is, that physics picking is handled asynchronously and all other input handling is done synchronously, which means, that Physics Picking has to happen last.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3915609445/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3917754222","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104933#issuecomment-3917754222","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104933","id":3917754222,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7phC9u","user":{"login":"iiiron","id":23551985,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNTUxOTg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23551985?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron","html_url":"https://github.com/iiiron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iiiron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-18T00:16:45Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T00:16:45Z","body":"I agree what adding a Control node that covers collision shape. When i code a game at first times it's very natural what i looking a way to create a Control that has customized shape not only rect\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---Original---\r\nFrom: \"Tomasz ***@***.***&gt;\r\nDate: Tue, Feb 17, 2026 22:58 PM\r\nTo: ***@***.***&gt;;\r\nCc: ***@***.******@***.***&gt;;\r\nSubject: Re: [godotengine/godot] _input_event of Area2D is impeded inSubviewportContainer (Issue #104933)\r\n\r\n\r\nKoBeWi left a comment (godotengine/godot#104933)\r\n  \r\nMaybe we should fix the problem that why setting mouse filter of SubviewportContainer to PASS, input event still swallowed like setting mouse filter STOP\r\n  \r\nSee #55432\r\n \r\nThis is expected behavior. What's IMO unexpected is that Controls always take priority over 2D nodes (is this even documented?). Right now you can't have both pickable Area2Ds and Controls in the scene. Maybe there could be a Viewport property that changes priority of physics picking (if it's feasible).\r\n \r\nProbably the best workaround for now is adding a Control node that covers the collision shape and connecting gui_input instead of input_event. However it works only for simple cases.\r\n \r\n—\r\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub, or unsubscribe.\r\nYou are receiving this because you authored the thread.Message ID: ***@***.***&gt;","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3917754222/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]